// The people of the Bocana waterfront and the rules for preparing the Garza (R1, D-022). Each person's
// skills, attributes, traits and languages are the truth. 'seeking' marks someone looking for a berth:
// what they ask, the least they will take, what they claim, when they give up, and whom they will not
// sail with. 'knows' is what a person says about others when asked; 'secrets' are seen, not told.
// Schedules are hour blocks [from, to), wrapping past midnight. Numbers are placeholders to tune.
// 'recognition' is how the port comes to know the expedition (R2e): greetings by standing, candidates
// coming to the captain. A person's 'greetings', 'claim' (a debt to collect from someone signed on) and
// 'farewell' (how they are seen off) are their own.
// 'weather' is the port's weather (R2d): each kind lasts minHours..maxHours, may begin only in
// [fromHour, toHour), and is followed by one of 'next' by weight. 'ambient' are small scenes the game
// plays out near the player, with no reward (PORT_EXPERIENCE §12); cells are [x, y] on the waterfront.
